From c514357fd284f1e0a6a2cce814f657baf1d855c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:57:10 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Profile: other regions' discs of the same executable
 (RegionRelease)

A profile can list another region's disc that holds its executable byte for
byte in its own encrypted EBOOT.BIN. The installer takes it and decrypts it
to the same executable, so the same corpus runs it. At start the framework
reads the disc id from the image; the save screens and save transfers use
that release's save folders, and the interface names the disc it is.
Textures and the ad hoc product code stay the profile's own.
---
